<title>GERMANY: East German Jan adjusted jobless rises 81,000.</title>
<headline>East German Jan adjusted jobless rises 81,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   Jan 97	 Dec 96	   Jan 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    1.393 million    1.187 million	1.257 million</p>
<p> Number (adj)		1.288 million    1.207 million	1.172 million</p>
<p> Change (adj)	     +81,000	+22,000	   +35,000</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		18.7 pct     15.9 pct	  16.8 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	68,174	 46,788	   81,428</p>
<p> Vacancies		   45,017	 48,923	   44,745</p>
<p> Change in number in work Nov 96	Oct 96</p>
<p>				-21,000	 -14,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
